@id n5_thomas
# DRAFT
# Thomas at dusk, on a bed in the infirmary, his head bandaged (night 5, clear and cold), after the dilemma.
# Brave about his "wound". Saved (n5_saved=thomas), he thanks the porter; passed over for Simon (n5_saved=simon), he's hurt
# and forgiving. His account of the attack points at the prior again. (The attack was staged. Nothing here says so.)
# Osric's face (osric_mask): keep quiet and eat Osric's bread tonight (Suspicion +5). What Simon told him: a frightened man
# names whoever you'll believe (Suspicion +10: the cult learns Simon talked). Simon scrubbing blood: he uses it.
# Claims: n5_thomas_attack (lie): the man in the mask was as tall as the prior.
== start
-> chose_me [if n5_saved=thomas]
-> chose_simon [if n5_saved=simon]
-> plain

== chose_me
(Thomas sits on the edge of a bed, his head bound in linen, a brown stain at the temple. He smiles when he sees you.)
Thomas {warm}: Alric. I'd be dead on the chapter house floor but for you. I'll not forget it.
Thomas {sad, still}: Poor Simon. I told you I'd seen him out at night. Whatever he'd got himself into, it came for him.
-> topics

== chose_simon
(Thomas sits on the edge of a bed, his head bound in linen, a brown stain at the temple. He looks at you, then smiles.)
Thomas {weary}: You went to Simon. I saw you choose, from the floor.
Thomas {warm, nod}: No, don't. You reached for the nearer man. I'm alive, as you see. I've a thick skull.
-> topics

== plain
(Thomas sits on the edge of a bed, his head bound in linen, a brown stain coming through at the temple.)
Thomas {warm}: Don't look so, Alric. A cut to the scalp bleeds like a pig and means nothing.
-> topics

== again
(Thomas has lain back against the wall with his eyes shut. He opens them when you come in.)
Thomas {weary}: Alric. Still here? Sit, if you like. I'm no use for anything else tonight.
-> topics

== topics
* [if not n5_thomas_attack] What happened in the chapter house, brother? -> attack
* [if osric_mask] [if not n5_thomas_osric] The hunter in the fog was Brother Osric. I saw his face. -> osric
* [if not n5_thomas_simon] What of Brother Simon? -> simon

== attack [set n5_thomas_attack]
Thomas {grave}: I heard Simon cry out and went in. A man in the mask was over him. Something struck me from behind. Then the floor.
-> n5_thomas_attack

# The attack was staged, and the men he points at are innocent (design doc, cast table): a lie.
== n5_thomas_attack [claim n5_thomas_attack lie]
Thomas {warm, still}: The one I saw was tall, Alric. As tall as the prior. I'll say no more than that, God forgive me if I'm wrong.
* [believe] God keep you, brother. I'll watch the prior. -> attack_believed
* [press] You were struck from behind, brother. How well did you see him? -> attack_pressed
* [confront osric_mask] The one in the fog last night wasn't the prior. It was Brother Osric. I saw his face. -> attack_broken

== attack_believed
Thomas {warm, nod}: Watch him, then. But say nothing to him. I've no proof, and he's the prior.
-> topics

== attack_pressed
Thomas {warm, still}: Well enough. In the door, before I was struck. I know what I saw, Alric.
Thomas {weary}: Let me rest now. My head.
-> topics

# The cult learns he knows (the game raises Suspicion). He doesn't confess: he turns it to Osric.
== attack_broken
(For a moment his face is nothing at all.)
Thomas {warm}: The prior was in my head, Alric. A man sees what he fears, in the dark.
-> osric [if not n5_thomas_osric]
-> topics

# He learns the porter knows Osric's face: Suspicion +5.
== osric [set n5_thomas_osric] [suspicion 5]
(He's very still.)
Thomas {grave}: Osric. Who carried the merchant from the pond. Who bakes our bread.
Thomas {warm, still}: Say nothing to him. Eat what he gives you tonight, and let him think you saw nothing.
Thomas {grave}: I'll think what's to be done.
-> topics

== simon [set n5_thomas_simon]
-> simon_dead [if died_simon]
-> simon_alive

== simon_dead
Thomas {sad, still}: I keep seeing him on those flags. A gentle soul, whatever he'd got into. I wish to God I'd been wrong about him.
-> simon_ask

== simon_alive
Thomas {warm}: How is he? He won't look at me. He hasn't since the chapter house.
-> simon_ask

== simon_ask
* [if n5_saved=simon] Brother Simon says you sent him to scrub the blood. -> simon_said
* [if simon_blood] I found Brother Simon scrubbing blood off the stones. -> simon_blood
* (Say nothing more about it.) -> topics

# Simon's word against him: the cult learns Simon talked (Suspicion +10).
== simon_said [set n5_thomas_simon_told=words] [suspicion 10]
(A long silence. He turns the bandage at his temple with one finger.)
Thomas {warm, still}: That I sent him. I've seen men in a fever name their own mothers, Alric.
Thomas {warm}: A frightened man says the name he thinks you'll believe, and he knows you trust me.
Thomas {grave}: Ask him where he was every night this week.
-> topics

== simon_blood [set n5_thomas_simon_told=blood]
-> blood_dead [if died_simon]
-> blood_alive

== blood_dead
(He shuts his eyes.)
Thomas {sad}: Scrubbing blood. Then he was in it, whatever it is. God rest him anyway.
-> topics

== blood_alive
Thomas {grave, still}: Scrubbing blood. Ask yourself why a man scrubs blood in the dark, and whose name he gives when he's caught.
-> topics

== leave
Thomas {warm, nod}: Sit by me at supper, Alric. I want a look at your eyes.
